---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StackUp from '../../../components/StackUp.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Tolerance Stack-Up Calculator"
  description="Linear worst-case and RSS tolerance stack-up with a Monte Carlo simulation, distribution histogram, and Cp/Cpk process capability. Runs entirely in your browser."
>
  <article class="tool-page wrap">
    <h1>Tolerance Stack-Up Calculator</h1>
    <p class="tool-intro">
      Build a dimensional chain from a list of contributing dimensions,
      each with its own tolerance and direction (adds to or subtracts
      from the stack). Get the worst-case and RSS (statistical) stack-up,
      run a 100,000-sample Monte Carlo simulation with a distribution
      histogram, and — if you enter spec limits — the fraction out of
      spec and Cp/Cpk process capability.
    </p>

    <StackUp />

    <div class="notice">
      The Monte Carlo simulation models each contributor as an independent
      normal distribution with standard deviation = tolerance / 3 (i.e.
      the stated tolerance is treated as a ±3σ spread) — a common
      convention, but an assumption about your actual process, not a
      measured fact. This tool runs entirely in your browser and is not a
      substitute for a full statistical tolerance analysis of your real
      process.
    </div>

    <p class="tool-footnote">
      Looking for GD&amp;T position tolerance instead of a dimensional
      chain? See the
      <a href="/calculators/true-position/">True Position &amp; Bonus Tolerance calculator</a>.
      See our <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> for what this tool is (and isn't)
      a substitute for.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
